Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Existence and branch qualifications", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"cdb3aecf-4990-4beb-be33-d43d53aa01aa"],

Cell["\<\
The coefficient matrix and its evolution operator have a finite epsilon->0 \
limit at generic kinematics. This does not by itself prove that a particular \
physical integral has a finite limit: its boundary constants may still \
contain 1/epsilon poles. The formulas require nonzero cutLambda values and a \
nondegenerate cut basis x0^2 x2^2 != 0. Powers, square roots and ArcTanh must \
be continued consistently if the integration contour leaves the displayed \
Euclidean branch or crosses a singular locus.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"5d1d669b-a09a-4cf1-ab5a-1802549203fd"],

